The MoNER corpus was constructed from publicly accessible Moroccan-dialect Wikipedia pages and publicly available YouTube comments. The licensing conditions of the two sources were considered separately. Wikipedia text is distributed under the CC BY-SA license.
For the YouTube component, the data were collected from publicly accessible comments in accordance with the applicable YouTube terms and policies. YouTube's policies emphasize compliance with applicable privacy requirements and the responsible handling, storage, and use of API data.
To reduce privacy risks, the MoNER resource does not include commenter names, channel identifiers, account information, or other direct identifiers of commenters. The annotations are used solely for research and benchmarking purposes. The dataset documentation also identifies the original source of the data and provides sufficient information to understand the provenance of the collected material without exposing commenter identities.
Because the corpus combines material originating from sources with different licensing conditions, the redistribution and licensing of the resulting resource are subject to the rights and terms applicable to each source. Users of the dataset are responsible for complying with the relevant source licenses, platform terms, and applicable privacy and copyright regulations.
